    "chunk_text": "13. Chairman, Sri Lanka Institute of Tourism and Hotel Management, Sri Lanka Convention Bureau\n\n14. Director General, Central Cultural Fund\n\n15. Director General, Department of Coastal Conservation\n\n16. Director General, Department of Irrigation\n\n17. Director General, Department of Wildlife\n\n19. Director General, Sri Lanka Tourism Development Authority\n\n20. Controller General, Department of Immigration and Emigration\n\n21. Director General, Mahaweli Development Authority\n\n22. Inspector General of Police, Police Department\n\n23. Duminda Hulangamuwa Esquire\n\n24. Krishan Balendra Esquire\n\n25. Nihal Muhandiram Esquire\n\n26. Nalin Jayasundara Esquire\n\n27. Suranjith Wevita Esquire\n\n28. Madam Shiromal Cooray\n\nGreetings!\n\nWHEREAS, public sector institutions and public-private partnership entities perform a pivotal catalytic role in the upgrading of tourism industry, the Government has recognized the necessity of a dedicated, empowered mechanism and a special program at the provincial, district and regional levels, for the proper coordination of existing institutions and the prompt transformation of the Sector,\n\nWHEREAS, the current Government, in pursuit of creating a thriving nation under the theme \u2018A Modernized Tourism Industry \u2013 An Attractive Destination\u2019, in line with the policy statement \u2018A Thriving Nation, a Beautiful Life\u2019, has accorded primary attention to expediting the realization of the aspirations and expectations of the public through activities relating to the development of tourism,\n\nWHEREAS, the Government has recognized the necessity of implementing a strategic program in an accurate and expeditious manner to promote the growth of the tourism industry, which has the potential to generate foreign exchange efficiently and expeditiously,"
