    "chunk_text": "22. Inspector General of Police, Police Department\n\n23. Duminda Hulangamuwa Esquire\n\n24. Krishan Balendra Esquire\n\n25. Nihal Muhandiram Esquire\n\n26. Nalin Jayasundara Esquire\n\n27. Suranjith Wevita Esquire\n\nas the members of the said Presidential Task Force to execute the below mentioned tasks subject to the provisions stipulated in the Constitution of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka and any other written laws.\n\nThe said tasks namely;\n\n1. Policy Analysis, Strategic Planning and Regulations\n\ni. Conduct policy analysis and provide recommendations on specific policy issues requiring specialized expertise. Identify a strategic framework for managing and promoting tourism activities, ensuring cultural heritage and environmental conservation, provide necessary guidance to relevant institutions to implement such strategies, in consultation with tourism experts and based on the existing situation.\n\nii. Carry out high-level national coordination and collaboration among relevant government institutions and stakeholders at the national, district, and divisional levels to implement the five-year (05) tourism plan.\n\niii. Develop policies, strategies and plans with the participation of various stakeholders, including the private sector.\n\niv. Develop human resources dedicated to tourism with public-private partnerships, public policies, visionary perspectives, public accountability and inspiration at leadership/decision-making levels.\n\nv. Provide guidance for the conduct of studies and related activities in the tourism sector.\n\nvi. Regulate the tourism sector effectively and formalize the engagement of all informal stakeholders.\n\nI fldgi ( ^I& fPoh - YS% ,xld m%cd;dka;s%l iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h - 2025'08'20Part I : Sec. (I) - GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA - 20.08.20254A\n\n2. Identification of Challenges and Proposal of Solutions"
  },
